Stubs that keep test/install-revert inside its fake HOME.

install/marvin reaches the desktop through helpers that talk to the running
shell over IPC (omarchy-shell and the omarchy-plugin-*/restart/theme wrappers
built on it) and through hyprctl. None of them read $HOME, so a test that only
sets HOME=$FAKE still reconfigures the developer's live session — running
./test/run once stripped every marvin.* widget out of a real shell.json.

The test puts this directory first on PATH so those calls land here instead.
pgrep is stubbed too, and only for `-x quickshell`: install/marvin gates its
IPC on shell_running(), and inside the sandbox the honest answer is "no shell".
Every other pgrep query is passed through to the real binary.
